Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-cci: reset retained controller state on runtime resume

Based on Birk Skyum's reset-on-resume proposal and the maintainer discussion:
https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/10/21/2473
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261020193946.51478-2-birk.skyum@pm.me

Backport adaptation for this older CCI driver: make reset completion IRQ
unmasking self-contained, reset unconditionally on resume, then restore
timing and the full interrupt mask. Propagate errors and disable clocks on
failure. Preserve the existing 1-second autosuspend policy; the proposed
50-ms timing workaround was explicitly withdrawn in the upstream thread.

--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-cci.c
@@ -227,6 +227,12 @@
 
 static int cci_reset(struct cci *cci)
 {
+	u32 mask;
+
+	/* Reset completion must also arrive after the power domain collapsed. */
+	mask = readl(cci->base + CCI_IRQ_MASK_0);
+	writel(mask | CCI_IRQ_MASK_0_RST_DONE_ACK, cci->base + CCI_IRQ_MASK_0);
+
 	/*
 	 * we reset the whole controller, here and for implicity use
 	 * master[0].xxx for waiting on it.
@@ -489,8 +495,14 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	cci_init(cci);
-	return 0;
+	/* A sensor power cycle can leave the clocked master unable to start. */
+	ret = cci_reset(cci);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = cci_init(cci);
+	if (ret)
+		cci_disable_clocks(cci);
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int __maybe_unused cci_suspend(struct device *dev)
